  "summary": "On June 11, 2026 Novo Nordisk disclosed unauthorized access to a limited number of internal IT systems from which data was copied externally, including pseudonymized clinical trial patient data (patient IDs, sex, year of birth, biomarkers, health and immunogenicity data) and healthcare provider contact details. The FulcrumSec gang claimed it got in around March using an Azure container registry credential exposed in a JavaScript bundle and a GitHub token, stayed for months, took about 1.3TB including AI models, drug discovery data and records of about 11,500 trial patients, demanded $25 million and began leaking data after Novo refused.",
